Sval: stack the macOS window buttons when their box stands vertically

The Workspace panel's narrowest layout is one column 48px wide, and the
window's close, minimize and zoom buttons stand in it, one over another.
A window-button box laid out in a vertical writing mode takes the
buttons' row turned on its side, and the window places each button down
that box: Gecko already places the close button through the frame
view's _closeButtonOrigin, and minimize and zoom, which otherwise follow
it in a row, get the same through _collapseButtonOrigin and
_zoomButtonOrigin. A box laid out horizontally keeps the system's row.

diff --git a/widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm b/widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm
